          "description": "PURPOSE: Read an unsigned 16-bit little-endian value from PSP memory at the given physical address. USAGE: Use for 16-bit game-state fields (most counters, IDs, small numerics). For single bytes use ppsspp_read8; for 32-bit use ppsspp_read32; for arbitrary byte spans use ppsspp_read_range. BEHAVIOR: No side effects — pure read. PSP is little-endian (MIPS Allegrex). Returns an error if address+2 exceeds the valid memory region. RETURNS: Single line",
